  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_last_cbd303e916fe1e3993eec958a71dbe958bf107eb5519fbbd8b22215d2a15e2f48c">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>Last (Latin lastus/lasta): a large unit of quantity, weight or packing whose size varied by commodity. As a measure of weight, c. 1870 kg (= 12 barrels); as a packing unit for liquid goods, usually 12 barrels; as a counting unit for hides, 200 pieces (= 20 dickers); for fish c. 1000 (croplings, herring, sprats); also used for eels, rye, soap, tar, pitch, butter, oil and bowstaves (24 bundles of 16 staves). Distinct from the shoemaker's last (a foot-shaped mould) and from lastage/ballast.</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
